.TH DSH-DESKTOP-DAEMON 1 "September 2026" "dsh-desktop 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dsh-desktop-daemon \- background service runner for DeepSeek Harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dsh-desktop-daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdsh-desktop-daemon\fR executes the DeepSeek Harness (@deepseek-ai/dsh) runtime
service with the Node.js internal exposure flag (\fB\-\-expose-internals\fR)
required for plugin hot module replacement (HMR).
.PP
\fBNote:\fR This daemon is normally managed and invoked by the systemd user
service \fBdsh-desktop.service\fR rather than started manually by hand.
.PP
Before launching the service, \fBdsh-desktop-daemon\fR verifies that the installed
Node.js and DeepSeek Harness versions meet runtime requirements, prepares the default
profile directory and manifest if missing, and ensures bundled package dependencies
are resolved.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSH_HOME
Base directory for DeepSeek Harness state, user profiles, and installed
plugins. When unset or empty, defaults to \fI~/.dsh\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dsh/
User runtime directory holding configuration, profiles, and plugins.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/dsh-desktop/
System installation directory containing the launcher, daemon executable,
and package helper binaries.
.TP
.I ~/.dsh/profiles/default/
Default user profile directory containing active plugin packages and configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.dsh/profiles/desktop-safe-mode/
Crash recovery safe-mode profile used to recover from incompatible plugins while
preserving shared credentials and workspace state.
.TP
.I ~/.dsh/profiles/.generations/
Content-addressed generation storage for installed plugins and projected symlinks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dsh-desktop (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
